<div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/General_Chemistry/Chemistry_2e_(OpenStax)/06:_Electronic_Structure_and_Periodic_Properties/6.03:_Development_of_Quantum_Theory" class="mt-section"><span id="Solution_4"></span><h6 class="lt-chem-414634 editable">Solution</h6>

<p class="lt-chem-414634">The table can be completed using the following rules:</p>

<ul data-bullet-style="bullet">
    <li class="lt-chem-414634">The orbital designation is \(nl\), where \(l = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, &hellip;\) is mapped to the letter sequence s, p, d, f, g, h, &hellip;,</li>
    <li class="lt-chem-414634">The \(m_l\) degeneracy is the number of orbitals within an l subshell, and so is \(2l + 1\) (there is one s orbital, three p orbitals, five d orbitals, seven f orbitals, and so forth).</li>
    <li class="lt-chem-414634">The number of radial nodes is equal to \(n &ndash; l &ndash; 1\).</li>
</ul>

